ZZPlug @VER@
==========

A small, zero-configuration USB stack for the MNT ZZ9000 (AmigaOS 3.1 or
newer, 68020 or better). Put a USB 2.0 hub on the ZZ9000's USB port, plug
your devices into it, and they work:

  mice         the pointer and buttons; the wheel and side buttons as
               NewMouse events
  keyboards    keys, qualifiers and repeat; Caps Lock and its light
  game pads    joystick port 2 for programs that use lowlevel.library, as a
               CD32 pad; ZZPlugPrefs sets each pad's buttons
  USB sticks   FAT sticks mount as USB0:, USB1:, ... (CrossDOS or fat95)
  hubs         USB 2.0 hubs, devices found and lost as they are plugged

Install: double-click Install_ZZPlug. It copies ZZPlug to C: and ZZPlugPrefs
to SYS:Prefs, puts this README and the test tools in a ZZPlug drawer where
you say, and starts ZZPlug at boot from S:User-Startup. Run it again to
update or to remove.

Needs: firmware 2.8 or newer on the ZZ9000 (USB proxy protocol version 2).
Mice, keyboards and game pads need a USB 2.0 hub between them and the
ZZ9000; USB sticks can also go straight into its port. ZZPlug
can't share the port with another USB stack (Poseidon): if one runs, ZZPlug
says so and does not start.

A hub plugged in when the Amiga is switched on is found only after it is
unplugged and plugged in again (a ZZ9000 firmware start-up issue,
zz9000-firmware#194); a warm reboot keeps it.

Using it, from a Shell:
  ZZPlug                   what is plugged in
  ZZPlug LIST VERBOSE      the same with addresses, speeds and endpoints
  ZZPlug START [QUIET]     run it
  ZZPlug STOP              stop it (refused while a USB stick is mounted)
  ZZPlug DIAG [ALL]        the ZZ9000 firmware's USB diagnostic page
  ZZPlug DUMP              record a device ZZPlug does not know yet, for
                           a bug report (or Record a device... in ZZPlugPrefs)

Games that read the joystick hardware directly (most WHDLoad games) don't see
a USB pad; programs that ask lowlevel.library do.

What is where:
  C/ZZPlug                     the USB stack (to C:)
  Prefs/ZZPlugPrefs            the prefs editor (to SYS:Prefs)
  Tools/JoyTest                prints what lowlevel.library reads from a port
  Tools/KeyTest                records every key a window gets
  LICENSE                      GNU GPL version 3

Source and bug reports: https://github.com/lainejones/ZZPlug
